I’m looking at a single pair measurement that shows a rate uncertainty of 0.02 shrinks to 0.004. This pair affects about 10% of targets, leading to a weighted risk reduction of around 0.1 compared to a denser query, which might be 0.03. That seems beneficial! I need to guide the candidate algorithm to favor suspect pairs likely to be the mode. However, the current half-size of 5 could mask the pair with unknown cross noise, reducing information by 25%. Running pair tests after the initial 20 could significantly improve things!
