**Calculating metrics for exponent variation**

I’m working on varying the exponent values from 0 to 3 to calculate the mean squared error (MSE) per fixture posterior. It seems I need to use the full dataset while focusing on the difference between the predicted values and the mean. However, I feel like the information I have may not be sufficient to grasp the entire distribution. I need to ensure I’m not missing important factors here!
